# ─── Raw harvest working files ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1.8 GB of supplier-sourced slab photography downloaded by harvest.py, plus the
# upscale scratch directory. These are INPUTS to the pipeline, not site assets —
# build_stones.py writes what the site actually serves into stones/ and assets/.
# They are also third-party photographs whose licensing is still an open question
# (see HANDOVER.md §7), which is a second reason they do not belong in a repo.
# ⚠️ These are `**/`-anchored ON PURPOSE. A gitignore pattern that contains a
# slash is anchored to the directory holding the .gitignore, and the site lives
# at `Topcat-Worktops-main/Website Demo/…`, not at the repo root — a plain
# `Website Demo/stones/…` pattern silently matches nothing and stages all 1.8 GB.
**/harvest/raw/
**/harvest/_upscale/

# ─── Local version control ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 58 dated snapshots of index.html at ~700 KB each, plus the handover snapshots.
# They exist only because this project had no git. Git replaces them — keeping
# both would put 44 MB of near-duplicate history in every clone.
*.bak
*.bak.md
*.pre-*.bak

# ─── OS / editor noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db

# ─── Agent session state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/

# ─── The upload folder ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `Website Demo/make_upload.py` writes a clean copy of the site here for the
# developer to drag onto the host (D289). It is 77 MB of files that already
# exist one directory up — a build artefact, not source.
**/upload/

# ─── The scroll film's 86 MB master ──────────────────────────────────────────
# D310. `assets/video/topcat-intro-1920.mp4` is the 11.7 MB file the site
# actually serves and it IS committed — the delivery flow is a clean clone plus
# `make_upload.py`, so anything the site loads has to be in here.
# The client's master (.mov, ProRes-sized, PCM audio) is kept beside the encode
# script that made it, on disk, but NOT in git: GitHub warns past 50 MB and hard
# blocks at 100, and a master nothing serves would be in every clone forever.
# ⛔ Do not delete it — a re-cut needs the master, not the encode (D241's rule).
**/assets/video/.src-*/*.mov
